# cw-tune-off: the CW page of the button bar with the CW tune widget OFF, the
# state the issue #122 reports ("the Tune widget does not appear on the CW band").
#
# The route is the user's: the KEY key loads the key pages (src/main_screen.c,
# KEYPAD_KEY -> buttons_load_page_group(buttons_group_key)) and the page button
# cycles to `page_cw_decoder_1` (src/buttons.cpp), the "(CW 1:2)" page that holds
# Decoder / Tuner / Dec SN R. The rig is in CW and the Tuner parameter is at its
# boot value (cw_tune=0, the port default, src/cfg/cfg.c), which is what the radio
# ships: the widget exists but update_visibility() (src/cw_tune_ui.c) keeps it
# hidden. scenario_settle codifies exactly that (the "(CW 1:2)" page, the "Tuner"
# button reading Off, the widget hidden), so the capture is the reported state and
# not a different page.
#
# The theme is the radio's own (Redshift), so the render matches the user's screen.

name cw-tune-off
screen cw-tune-off

theme Redshift
seed 20

frequency_hz 7030000
tx_frequency_hz 7030000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode cw
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
